rget=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T17:34:59-07:00","id":249317,"title":"","content":"Do you think a vampire could save herself from a fall with Weightless Step? It seems like a thematic effect, leaping off of something impossibly tall and landing safely and silently. On Wings of Shadow can definitely do it, but this would be less than full flight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T17:41:05-07:00","id":249322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Smarmy Vamp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/249243-subvolo-the-discipline-of-flight?p=249317#post249317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you think a vampire could save herself from a fall with Weightless Step? It seems like a thematic effect, leaping off of something impossibly tall and landing safely and silently. On Wings of Shadow can definitely do it, but this would be less than full flight.</div> </div> </div> </div>O_O<br /> <br /> Yes. +1. Wow, Much Good. Added.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T18:00:24-07:00","id":249328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/249243-subvolo-the-discipline-of-flight?p=249281#post249281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Double thanks.<br /> <br /> If there are any weird flight/kinesis powers you think belong please let me know. Except Force Choke, that's just played out.</div> </div> </div> </div>It not TK, its obfuscate for gravity.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T18:14:48-07:00","id":249337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Smarmy Vamp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/249243-subvolo-the-discipline-of-flight?p=249317#post249317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you think a vampire could save herself from a fall with Weightless Step? It seems like a thematic effect, leaping off of something impossibly tall and landing safely and silently. On Wings of Shadow can definitely do it, but this would be less than full flight.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/249243-subvolo-the-discipline-of-flight?p=249322#post249322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">O_O<br /> <br /> Yes. +1. Wow, Much Good. Added.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would make for a very cool escape, <br /> <br /> He's pursers were catching up to him,they had sealed all the exits,he was traped.It would only be a matter of time before they found him and took him to their master. He had to escape, he had to tell the prince of the Owl. So he took the only logical choice, he opened a window and as they came through the door jump. As he fell he looked back to his pursuers and look at them. They were frightened, they would probably going to die for not catching him. He felt pity for that but better them than him. Over three weeks of being chased,now he's free, so he laugh and he kept on laughing all the way down the Empire State Building","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":3742,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","user":"Iceblade44","date":". 09-04-2014, 10:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T18:38:04-07:00","id":249353,"title":"","content":"Is the second dot contested when rolled against a &quot;being&quot;? Once lifted by the fourth dot, are victims powerless to do anything about it? I suggest change the &quot;out of waves of weightless force&quot; to &quot;waves of weightlessness&quot;; it corrects a typo + talking about a wave of any kind of force is odd when the very sentence before it says the discipline generates no force whatsoever.<br /> <br /> Wouldn't Celerity be more appropriate than vigor for crow's cunning? Vigor is linked to strength, I don't see it affecting fine control much. Celerity seems, out of the three physical disciplines, most closely linked to dexterity, so that seems appropriate. You have one devotion for each physical discipline so I'm assuming that's deliberate, but I'm really not quite seeing it.<br /> <br /> I like the flavour of the discipline, it'll be fun to see it working in play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":1292,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","user":"Unahim","date":". 09-04-2014, 09:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T19:09:48-07:00","id":249372,"title":"","content":"Come to think of it, why is Flight so difficult to get one's hands on in the WoD? I once heard that when a vampire unlocked flight, they &quot;win the game&quot;.<br /> <br /> I would think in a world that has guns and long ranged powers, this wouldn't be that big of an issue. Unless you're doing a Dark Ages campaign. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T19:31:20-07:00","id":249391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/249243-subvolo-the-discipline-of-flight?p=249353#post249353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the second dot contested when rolled against a &quot;being&quot;? Once lifted by the fourth dot, are victims powerless to do anything about it? I suggest change the &quot;out of waves of weightless force&quot; to &quot;waves of weightlessness&quot;; it corrects a typo + talking about a wave of any kind of force is odd when the very sentence before it says the discipline generates no force whatsoever.<br /> <br /> Wouldn't Celerity be more appropriate than vigor for crow's cunning? Vigor is linked to strength, I don't see it affecting fine control much. Celerity seems, out of the three physical disciplines, most closely linked to dexterity, so that seems appropriate. You have one devotion for each physical discipline so I'm assuming that's deliberate, but I'm really not quite seeing it.<br /> <br /> I like the flavour of the discipline, it'll be fun to see it working in play.</div> </div> </div> </div>In order of points given:<ul><li>Second dot is now penalized by Supernatural Advantage. It's also really easy to break out of if your a living thing. Just kick the ground or grab a wall and you can wrench yourself free.</li> <li>Victims lifted by the 4th dot are &quot;helpless&quot; in the sense that they are lifted, but still not without options. Ranged attacks, disciplines, allies, negotiation, they have plenty of avenues to escape. With powers like Mesmerize, Charm, and Face of the Beast this is actually among the less disabling disciplines.</li> <li>Suggestion taken, typo fixed.</li> <li>Celerity is the discipline of speed, not delicacy, and with Crow's Cunning the vampire is generating genuine force to move individual parts. So I felt Vigor was appropriate. Also I wanted a power that had a Vigor prereq.</li> </ul>Thanks for the feedback, this discipline has actually seen a bit of play on an antagonist. It was deemed terrifying, but in each encounter the players managed to overcome it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T19:58:32-07:00","id":249403,"title":"","content":"Love it, really great way to bring that sort of vampiric power into 2nd edition.<br /> <br /> I like the idea of giving it to some of the Julii. Maybe there's a particular lineage of them who have internalized the power, or maybe there's just a number of Julii elders who know it. Either way, makes an awesome power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T20:48:35-07:00","id":249440,"title":"","content":"PenDragon, you are my homebrew hero. I love how you've captured the <i>feel</i> of Vampiric flight being this stately thing, and their pseudo-telekinesis being imperious rather than simply &quot;powerful.&quot; For abilities so like Mage's Forces superficially, they're very different in tone and style.<br /> <br /> Quick question, though: shouldn't <i>Invisible Hand</i> / <i>Gentle Talon</i> be Dex + Larc + Subvolo vs &lt;Resist Stat&gt; + &lt;Power Stat&gt;? All other save-or-suck style powers are done that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-05T01:37:45-07:00","id":249639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/249243-subvolo-the-discipline-of-flight?p=249440#post249440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">PenDragon, you are my homebrew hero. I love how you've captured the <i>feel</i> of Vampiric flight being this stately thing, and their pseudo-telekinesis being imperious rather than simply &quot;powerful.&quot; For abilities so like Mage's Forces superficially, they're very different in tone and style.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aw shucks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/249243-subvolo-the-discipline-of-flight?p=249440#post249440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quick question, though: shouldn't <i>Invisible Hand</i> / <i>Gentle Talon</i> be Dex + Larc + Subvolo vs &lt;Resist Stat&gt; + &lt;Power Stat&gt;? All other save-or-suck style powers are done that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>I tossed this about quite a bit, make it resisted? Make it contested? While the power is, as you put it, Save or Suck it is much less debilitating than the one dot Mesmerize or two dot Face of the Beast, both of which can completely shut a character down. At least with this the lifted character still retains agency, she can act, attack, struggle. Sure it's a bad situation, but as I said, my own players were subjected to this thrice and each time they weaseled their way out.<br /> <br /> However, for the sake of the roll, and for those players who don't like creative problem solving I will acquiesce. The power certainly shouldn't be resisted, it doesn't really count successes. So I'll tweak it to Stamina + Sup Tol. Statistically the roll still strongly favors the Vampire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-05T15:11:26-07:00","id":250170,"title":"","content":"I don't think it's really fair to shoehorn people who want the activation roll to resemble similar powers in with people who &quot;don't like creative problem solving&quot;. It sounds a bit belittling, intended or not. I don't think the two examples of possible ways to break free (kicking the ground or pushing against a wall) are all that creative either, they're rather straightforward ways to deal with it that would be immediately obvious, but they only work if the Subvolo user didn't consider to move you away from those possibilities straight away. It's not as much a thing you do to get free, as a thing the user forgets to prevent.<br /> <br /> Also, from the way the discipline is written, they wouldn't even work. You're not being struck by an external force if you're pushing a wall, right? Unless we're getting really physics up in here, for every force exerted an equal counter force, and so on and so on, but that's not quite &quot;struck by&quot;. Maybe clarify to &quot;whenever you're struck by an external force or forced to move at a speed past walking pace by influences outside of the discipline&quot;, just to prevent confusion.<br /> <br /> If I'm dealing with a competent subvolo user who's blocking off the easy solutions, I might try to throw an object straight up and hit myself with it. If it hits me hard enough that might work. If he doesn't subvolo catch it before it does. I can't really think of another way to do it, except maybe tying all your clothes together into some form of grappling hook and then pulling yourself free by hooking it into something. That wouldn't work if he was at al paying attention. It doesn't sound that much easier to get out than Mesmerize, to be honest. Stab yourself to get out of Mesmerized between the point where he does it and gives the command, and don't look at his eyes. There seem to be advantages and disadvantages to both, so making the initial roll about equally likely to succeed doesn't seem like a stretch to me.<br /> <br /> Do victims get defense when subvolo'd? What about celerity?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-05T15:51:42-07:00","id":250188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/249243-subvolo-the-discipline-of-flight?p=250170#post250170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think it's really fair to shoehorn people who want the activation roll to resemble similar powers in with people who &quot;don't like creative problem solving&quot;. It sounds a bit belittling, intended or not. I don't think the two examples of possible ways to break free (kicking the ground or pushing against a wall) are all that creative either, they're rather straightforward ways to deal with it that would be immediately obvious, but they only work if the Subvolo user didn't consider to move you away from those possibilities straight away. It's not as much a thing you do to get free, as a thing the user forgets to prevent.<br /> <br /> Also, from the way the discipline is written, they wouldn't even work. You're not being struck by an external force if you're pushing a wall, right? Unless we're getting really physics up in here, for every force exerted an equal counter force, and so on and so on, but that's not quite &quot;struck by&quot;. Maybe clarify to &quot;whenever you're struck by an external force or forced to move at a speed past walking pace by influences outside of the discipline&quot;, just to prevent confusion.<br /> <br /> If I'm dealing with a competent subvolo user who's blocking off the easy solutions, I might try to throw an object straight up and hit myself with it. If it hits me hard enough that might work. If he doesn't subvolo catch it before it does. I can't really think of another way to do it, except maybe tying all your clothes together into some form of grappling hook and then pulling yourself free by hooking it into something. That wouldn't work if he was at al paying attention. It doesn't sound that much easier to get out than Mesmerize, to be honest. Stab yourself to get out of Mesmerized between the point where he does it and gives the command, and don't look at his eyes. There seem to be advantages and disadvantages to both, so making the initial roll about equally likely to succeed doesn't seem like a stretch to me.<br /> <br /> Do victims get defense when subvolo'd? What about celerity?</div> </div> </div> </div>Adjusted the wording on Invisible Hand, kicking a wall or grabbing a sign-post would absolutely end the two dot effect. Breaking The Gentle Talon would require a successful Strength + Athletics roll to contest. Athletics is no longer added to defense, but as the character can still squirm and move they are not completely helpless. This too has been added to the doc.<br /> <br /> As for getting out, no, The Gentle Talon isn't easy to escape. But that's not really what I meant when I said 'debilitating'. Mesmerize shuts down the characters actions (and I totally would not allow a character to stab himself to escape being Mesmerized, the Condition starts when eye contact is met not when an order is given), Face of the Beast forces them to run. With The Gentle Talon the character retains agency and, as you noted above, can take actions to free himself or harm the vampire. Will they always succeed? No, sometimes you're just fucked. But that's nothing new to WoD.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit: </b>With regards to Celerity, obvious the character can't move so the speed boost and dodge options are out, but it continues to be added to Defense and they can still take interrupt actions to attack/grapple/get creative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-05T15:55:14-07:00","id":250194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/249243-subvolo-the-discipline-of-flight?p=250170#post250170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stab yourself to get out of Mesmerized between the point where he does it and gives the command, and don't look at his eyes.</div> </div> </div> </div>This makes me sad<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Athletics is no longer added to defense, but as the character can still squirm and move they are not completely helpless.</div> </div> </div> </div>This makes me happy.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-05T18:50:22-07:00","id":250273,"title":"","content":"What about a flat defense penalty? Dexterity is for a large part reaction time, sure, but the other part is flexibility and finesse of motion. These last two are also contained in the athletics skill. If this flexibility cannot be brought into play due to the discipline, then for me it feels weird that dexterity's rating is not affected. Someone more used to moving their body (athletics) should still have the advantage to figuring out how all of this works in a weightless state compared to someone who hasn't got the faintest clue. If you're able to push and pull objects, you should be able to kick up your legs and curling yourself into a ball, dodging that sword swinged at your legs. That would be something a trained gymnast might think about. Maybe a flat -3 to defense would work best, giving the same average penalty as &quot;no athletics&quot; would, but keeping the defense values of a dex 1, atl 3 and dex 3 atl 1 character the same, assuming corresponding wits scores.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-07T13:48:22-07:00","id":251694,"title":"","content":"My thought process upon seeing this thread: 'A flight Discipline? Surely that'll be poorly thought out with all the later dots rendering earlier ones useless... Oh, wait, it's Pendragon. Yeah, looks good.'","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-07T15:36:34-07:00","id":251745,"title":"","content":"Nobody answered my question<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-07T16:13:08-07:00","id":251753,"title":"","content":"Fiiiiine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/249243-subvolo-the-discipline-of-flight?p=249372#post249372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Come to think of it, why is Flight so difficult to get one's hands on in the WoD? I once heard that when a vampire unlocked flight, they &quot;win the game&quot;.<br /> <br /> I would think in a world that has guns and long ranged powers, this wouldn't be that big of an issue. Unless you're doing a Dark Ages campaign. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>This is a complicated question, plenty of reasons, but I can assure you that &quot;being game winning&quot; is not among them. One can hardly 'win' a story after all, and closest flight comes is the ability to escape some conflicts (just some), which isn't so much winning as it is refusing to play. <br /> <br /> Personally I find flight a pretty boring power, fun in concept but not terribly useful on its own. If you look at fictional characters who can fly it's always supported by some other ability, and generally takes back seat to their true power. Especially in a modern setting with guns, cars and convenient fire escapes the value of being able to fly is pretty limited. It doesn't solve a lot of problems, it doesn't help in social or mental scenarios, and it's only conditionally useful in a fight. Hence why I merged flight with telekinesis when creating the subvolo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-08T01:20:13-07:00","id":252087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/249243-subvolo-the-discipline-of-flight?p=249372#post249372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Come to think of it, why is Flight so difficult to get one's hands on in the WoD? I once heard that when a vampire unlocked flight, they &quot;win the game&quot;.<br /> <br /> I would think in a world that has guns and long ranged powers, this wouldn't be that big of an issue. Unless you're doing a Dark Ages campaign. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Flight certaintly does not win the game, but its a nice boon to have. Also it is not a difficult power to get, Protean allows flight already in many different ways. You can glide with its second dot, and have full winged flight(at double your base speed) with the fourth dot. If we count the shapeshifting as well, Protean 3 grants flight, there is the merit that allows you to turn into a swarm of something, so flight and finally Protean 5, you can fly with this one too.<br /> <br /> <br /> On the topic of Subvolo, amazing work PenDragon. Really amazing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3669,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3669-blackheartz","user":"blackheartz","date":". 09-08-2014, 05:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3669-blackheartz","name":"blackheartz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3669_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-08T07:51:21-07:00","id":252310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackheartz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/249243-subvolo-the-discipline-of-flight?p=252087#post252087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Flight certaintly does not win the game, but its a nice boon to have. Also it is not a difficult power to get, Protean allows flight already in many different ways. You can glide with its second dot, and have full winged flight(at double your base speed) with the fourth dot. If we count the shapeshifting as well, Protean 3 grants flight, there is the merit that allows you to turn into a swarm of something, so flight and finally Protean 5, you can fly with this one too.<br /> <br /> <br /> On the topic of Subvolo, amazing work PenDragon. Really amazing.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, they were referring to the Tremere, when they said that. But I think the Circle could just as easily fulfill that role if you're hanging out of reach, dropping blood rituals on people. Hee hee.<br /> <br /> But yeah, like I said, it doesn't really seem like it should be all that rare of a power. I like the first level of this discipline too, because it reminds of movies where the vampire just starts walking up the side of a wall casually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-08T10:33:21-07:00","id":252470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackheartz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Flight certaintly does not win the game, but its a nice boon to have. Also it is not a difficult power to get, Protean allows flight already in many different ways. You can glide with its second dot, and have full winged flight(at double your base speed) with the fourth dot. If we count the shapeshifting as well, Protean 3 grants flight, there is the merit that allows you to turn into a swarm of something, so flight and finally Protean 5, you can fly with this one too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's not forget Blood Sorcery either. I can think of several ways for Cruac to present flight, from conjured steeds to <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baba_Yaga\" target=\"_blank\">flying pestles</a>.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/249243-subvolo-the-discipline-of-flight?p=252310#post252310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But yeah, like I said, it doesn't really seem like it should be all that rare of a power. I like the first level of this discipline too, because <b>it reminds of movies where the vampire just starts walking up the side of a wall casually</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bingo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-30T09:28:01-08:00","id":326092,"title":"","content":"I just logged in to praise you, PenDragon.Well done. I love the feel of the powers and its aesthetics, and of course that introduction; really good stuff. But, i have one thing to request.<br /> Bring us a classy and aristocratic use of Subvolo merged with Resilience! The obvious choice is creating a shield, but that feel a lot like telekinesis...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-30T09:36:38-08:00","id":326097,"title":"","content":"Oh, hey, turns out I haven't commented on how cool this is either.<br /> <br /> Hey, Pen, this is pretty cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-30T19:36:09-08:00","id":326531,"title":"","content":"This is awesome, and you should feel awesome for making it! The visuals are awesome, and I imagine anyone with the always on power &quot;non-magic locks don't work&quot; would be a formidable foe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T11:01:15-08:00","id":327187,"title":"","content":"Aww, such praise. I'm blushing here.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Bring us a classy and aristocratic use of Subvolo merged with Resilience! The obvious choice is creating a shield, but that feel a lot like telekinesis... </div> </div> </div>How can I turn down a request like that?<br /> <br /> <b>Inviolate Air (Subvolo \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Resilience \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> Cost: 1 Vitae<br /> Dice Pool: Dexterity + Athletics + Subvolo<br /> Action: Reflexive<br /> Duration: [Successes] Actions<br /> <br /> Slings and arrows cannot mar the sky, why so should they harm the crow? With a wave of his hand the vampire dismisses all ranged attacks. Any small projectile (size 0-3) that comes within a few yards of the vampire grinds to a halt, left to drift harmlessly in the air. Attacks performed in extreme close combat and projectiles with internal propulsion (e.g. rockets) are unaffected. All other ranged attacks fail completely, and will do no harm to those within the vampire's protective bubble.<br /> <i>This Devotion Costs 3 Experiences to Learn.</i><br /> <br /> Also added to <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1q3dMgL9v7Vryw-uvWzJ8meJrvvQDjGD6_vjJLPGCjso/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">the doc</a>.<br /> <br /> Edit: I'm feeling inspired, have three more Devotions:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Silent Embrace (Subvolo \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Obfuscate \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> Cost: None<br /> <br /> Like the wings of an owl subtle forces steal away sound, silencing victims for their sojourn to the clouds. With this devotion a vampire can implement Obfuscate remotely, anyone she could nab with The Gentle Talon is a viable target. Similarly, assuming her blood potency allows it, she may use the Gentle Talon and Touch of Shadow as one combined action, silencing and snatching simultaneously.<br /> <i>This Devotion costs 3 Experiences to Learn.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Ascendant Familiar (Subvolo \u2022\u2022\u2022, Animalism \u2022\u2022)</b><br /> Cost: +1 Vitae, Enhances Raise the Familiar<br /> <br /> Logic would dictate that Subvolo masters would select similarly exalted companions, but that needn't be so. With the blessing of the crow any beast may stalk the sky. By spending an additional point of Vitae while creating a familiar the vampire blesses it with the gift of Subvolo. Hence forward the familiar can fly, constantly affected by Weightless Step and enhanced by On Wings of Shadow.<br /> <i>This Devotion costs 2 Experiences to Learn.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Firmament Reign (Subvolo \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Animalism \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 or Obfuscate \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> Cost: None<br /> <br /> It is said the first crows made their havens on mountain peaks and atop towering trees, removed from earthly concerns and furnished with stolen finery. The truth of these tales is suspect, but the possibility is there. With this devotion the vampire extends the powers of subvolo across his entire domain, anywhere he has claimed through Lord of the Land or Oubliette. Within his powers are enduring, lasting indefinitely so long as the territory is his. Moreover all powers of Subvolo come more easily, enjoying a 1 Vitae discount to activation (minimum 0).<br /> <i>This Devotion costs 5 Experiences to Learn</i>.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 12-01-2014, 03:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T13:06:26-08:00","id":327339,"title":"","content":"Take my like and my love, sir. Well done. I'll keep thinking about new devotions for this amazing Discipline. By the way,i'd say there's enough love for the Bloodline script, wouldn't you say? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T13:08:51-08:00","id":327341,"title":"","content":"I had been a while that I don't post/comment a thing over here... but Subvolo is very very noteworthy, I just felt compeled to do it, so: Congrats Pendragon!<br /> <br /> By the way... now that you gave birth to your little monster... there is any bloodline in your schems? (I know that must be something more...)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/646-mabafu","name":"mabafu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar646_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T14:36:45-08:00","id":327374,"title":"","content":"Feedback like this is just so heartening. Have another devotion<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>The Silken Hand (Subvolo \u2022\u2022, Majesty \u2022\u2022)*</b><br /> Cost: 1 Vitae<br /> Dice Pool: Presence + Expression + Subvolo vs Composure + Supernatural Advantage<br /> Action: Instant<br /> <br /> The grip of Subvolo is one of terrible, stomach pitting helplessness. But mix in a Daeva's saccharine smile and that weightlessness becomes euphoric. Her attention gripped with a simple gesture, the victim is drawn in, sliding weightlessly (as though affected by Weightless Step) to the vampire's side. She gains the Charmed Condition, and a small degree of Subvolo's power. So long as his victim remains Charmed the vampire may carry her as though weightless, and share the effects of Weightless Step and On Wings of Shadow while in physical contact.<br /> <i>This Devotion Costs 2 Experiences to Learn</i><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>*A nearly identical version of this Devotion exists, named The Iron Hand. Adapted by Ventrue it requires one dot of Dominate instead of two Majesty, inflicts the Mesmerized Condition, and uses a dice pool of Intelligence + Intimidation + Subvolo.</b></span> </div> </div> </div>As for a Bloodline, the fluff of Subvolo is that it belonged to a lost clan, the Kindred of the Sky, who may or may not have become strix. There's clearly demand for <b>something, </b>perhaps the Kindred of the Sky deserve a full write-up...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 12-01-2014, 05:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T16:29:56-08:00","id":327478,"title":"","content":"Awesome work! As for bloodlines, the Tengu you mention might also work... Or some sort of Gargoyle bloodline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-02T05:50:05-08:00","id":328103,"title":"","content":"You know,<b>The Silken Hand</b> reminds me powerfully of Wendy and Peter Pan and that feeling of bliss and awe. And i'm thinking about that final description in one and each of the Clans in the new B&amp;S basic book,the one who always talks about the Kindred in a Snow White light. Liiiike it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"